:174-179](skills/shared/subskill-invocation.md), [skills/design/SKILL.md:46-48](skills/design/SKILL.md) vs plan Step 5b snippet — Inline `print \"**⚠ …**\"` for rename/publish conflicts the nested artifact-only contract (human-readable lines forbidden when `SESSION_ENV_PATH` is set). **Suggested revision:** Gate those prints on standalone mode or log to `execution-issues.md` / file-backed sidecar per nested rules.\n\n4. **[code-quality]** [scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh:11-13](scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh), [scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh:31-34](scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh) — Plan lists code edits but not the in-file usage banner or the “Rename semantics” comment that still documents three lifecycle prefixes. **Suggested revision:** Extend the file list to include these comment blocks so agents do not ship stale contracts.\n\n5. **[architecture]** [plan.txt:108-110](plan.txt) (merge design) — Default path uses `gh pr merge --admin --delete-branch`, which needs elevated token rights and deletes the remote head branch; this is heavier than “flush logs” suggests. **Suggested revision:** Call out fork/contributor and org-policy limitations in docs; consider an opt-out or “open PR only” mode as a follow-up.\n\n6. **[security]** [plan.txt:35-38](plan.txt), [plan.txt:126](plan.txt) — `--admin` merge intentionally bypasses branch protection and CI; redaction is best-effort. **Suggested revision:** In `SECURITY.md` / script sibling, tie admin-merge to trusted-operator assumption and restate secret-handling limits (plan already mentions keys in prompts; link merge privilege to same section).\n\n7. **[code-quality]** [plan.txt:72-84](plan.txt) — Using `grep` for `PUBLISH_OK=false` / `FAILED=true` is brittle if unrelated output contains those substrings. **Suggested revision:** Parse `emit_kv` lines or rely on exit status plus a single sentinel line from helpers.\n\n**[OUT_OF_SCOPE]** [scripts/tracking-issue-write.md:1-11](scripts/tracking-issue-write.md) — Rename usage table should gain `planned`; not listed in the plan’s modify list; include in same change set to avoid contract drift.\n\n**[OUT_OF_SCOPE]** [docs/issue-anchored-plan.md:177-245](docs/issue-anchored-plan.md) — Narrative around tracking-issue `IN PROGRESS` may deserve a clarifying note if `[PLANNED]` becomes a visible post-design state; avoids confusion for implement preflight vs design completion.\n\n**Creative alternative (architecture):** Instead of auto-merge with `--admin`, default to “commit + push + open PR” and emit `PR_URL` for manual merge when policy forbids admin merges—preserves logs without privileged tokens; auto-merge stays behind a flag.\n\nI will not output `{\"no_issues_found\": true}` because we have findings.","session_id":"f024153d-1a8e-4dbe-81ca-7fde22351bd6","request_id":"1aeb1993-c315-4ad0-a8d3-d91c81d9af9d","usage":{"inputTokens":97202,"outputTokens":7033,"cacheReadTokens":307968,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
