<TMPDIR>/codex-sketch-pragmatic-output.txt.sidecar:4706:I would keep this as a narrow `/design` completion extension, not a redesign of the run-log system. Add `planned -> [PLANNED] ` to [scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh](<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh) and teach [scripts/lib-title-markers.sh](<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/scripts/lib-title-markers.sh) to treat `[PLANNED]` as a managed lifecycle prefix. In [skills/design/SKILL.md](<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/skills/design/SKILL.md), Step 5 should remain the single completion boundary: after `plan-block-write.sh` succeeds, run `tracking-issue-write.sh rename --state planned`, then flush design logs, create/merge the log PR, and only then call `cleanup-tmpdir.sh`. Title rename should be best-effort but visible, consistent with existing terminal rename behavior.
