ge line and tracking-issue-write.sh header usage and rename semantics prose for planned and PLANNED\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcorrectness\tplan artifact skills/design insertion (see plan.txt:76-87)\tUses scripts/design-log-publish.sh without CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT\tCWD outside repo root breaks publish\tSpell invocations as \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/design-log-publish.sh\" like other Step 5 tools\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tarchitecture\tMakefile:72-80:663-664\tPlan says wire harness into make lint but omits which test-harnesses shard should own the new target\tMaintainers must guess CI shard placement\tAdd a test-design-log-publish target with harness-timer and register it on a specific test-harnesses-N dependency line\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tarchitecture\t.claude/rules/script-md-siblings.md:19-26\tNew scripts/test-*.sh harness without a sibling stub\tContradicts the repo script documentation sibling rule\tAdd scripts/test-design-log-publish.md stub pointing at scripts/design-log-publish.md\n1\tin_scope\tlatent\trisk-integration\tskills/design/SKILL.md:179\tClarify-router success path writes the plan then Step 5 hygiene without the new rename and log flush steps\tDesign completes via clarify with inconsistent title and log retention behavior\tDocument whether 5b rename and design-log-publish run on the clarify-only exit or remain main accept-only flow\n\n[OUT_OF_SCOPE] **architecture** — [CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) (~4629-4630) narrative lists rename states as in-progress|done|stalled only; updating it is user-visible release documentation outside the written file list.\n\n1. **correctness** — [`skills/design/SKILL.md`](skills/design/SKILL.md):163-168 — The plan states `SESSION_ID` is parsed in Step 0, but Step 0 currently only requires parsing `SESSION_TMPDIR` and reviewer flags, so `--run-id` for `design-log-publish.sh` has no grounded source. **Suggested revision:** Extend Step 0 parsing to include `SESSION_ID` from `session-setup.sh` output (see [`scripts/session-setup.sh`](scripts/session-setup.sh):282-283) and thread it into Step 5.\n\n2. **risk-integration** — [`skills/design/SKILL.md`](skills/design/SKILL.md):48-92, :784-785, :851-853 — Proposed `print` warnings and captured publish output conflict with the nested artifact-only contract and with the rule that exactly one terminal machine footer is the last output line when `PLAN_WRITE_OK=true`. **Suggested revision:** Gate user-visible warnings on empty `SESSION_ENV_PATH`, avoid printing raw `publish_out` in nested mode, and order operations so the machine footer remains strictly last.\n\n3. **risk-integration** — [`skills/design/SKILL.md`](skills/design/SKILL.md):805-812 — Plan snippets pass `--repo \"$REPO\"` but the design skill does not define `REPO` in Step 0 or Step 5. **Suggested revision:** Resolve `REPO` once via [`scripts/resolve-repo.sh`](scripts/resolve-repo.sh) (same pattern documented in [`skills/fix-issue/scripts/find-lock-issue.md`](skills/fix-issue/scripts/find-lock-issue.md):7) and document it beside `ISSUE_NUMBER`.\n\n4. **architecture** — [`scripts/create-pr.sh`](scripts/create-pr.sh):4-5, :110-115 — `create-pr.sh` opens a PR from the current branch head, so `gh pr merge` merges the full branch delta to the base, not merely the path-limited log commit described in the plan. **Suggested revision:** Fork an ephemeral logs-only branch from the integration tip, cherry-pick or commit only logs there, or explicitly document and enforce that the feature branch has no extra commits before auto-merge.\n\n5. **correctness** — [`scripts/larch-log.sh`](scripts/larch-log.sh):124-137 vs plan edge cases — Plan text says refusing on `main` while `larch-log.sh commit` uses `current_branch_is_default` (`main`, `master`, and `origin/HEAD` default). **Suggested revision:** Reuse that full predicate for `design-log-publish.sh`, not a `main`-only check.\n\n6. **correctness** — [`skills/fix-issue/scripts/find-lock-issue.sh`](skills/fix-issue/scripts/find-lock-issue.sh):137-149, :854-863 — Managed-prefix gates omit `[PLANNED]`, so product semantics for `/fix-issue` eligibility versus design-completed issues are undefined. **Suggested revision:** Decide whether `[PLANNED]` is machine-owned like the other prefixes; if yes, extend `has_managed_lifecycle_prefix` and error messaging and add harness coverage.\n\n7. **code-quality** — [`scripts/tracking-issue-write.md`](scripts/tracking-issue-write.md):9; [`scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh`](scripts/tracking-issue-write.sh):12-40, :97-104 — Contract files still document only `in-progress|done|stalled`. **Suggested revision:** Update the `.md` usage line and the shell header rename semantics block when adding `planned`.\n\n8. **correctness** — Plan snippet at [`plan.txt`](file:///Users/zhupanov/.cache/larch/sessions/claude-design-larch5-QhAbWK/plan.txt):76-87 — Invokes `scripts/design-log-publish.sh` without `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`. **Suggested revision:** Match [`skills/design/SKILL.md`](skills/design/SKILL.md):810-811 style for all new script invocations.\n\n9. **architecture** — [`Makefile`](Makefile):72-80, :663-664 — The plan says wire the new harness into `make lint` but does not name which `test-harnesses-*` shard should depend on it. **Suggested revision:** Add `test-design-log-publish` with `harness-timer.sh` and register it on a specific shard line.\n\n10. **architecture** — [`.claude/rules/script-md-siblings.md`](.claude/rules/script-md-siblings.md):19-26 — A new `scripts/test-design-log-publish.sh` should get a sibling stub `.md` per repo rules. **Suggested revision:** Add `scripts/test-design-log-publish.md` pointing at the primary contract in `scripts/design-log-publish.md`.\n\n11. **risk-integration** — [`skills/design/SKILL.md`](skills/design/SKILL.md):179 — The clarify success path performs `plan-block-write` and Step 5 hygiene without the new rename and log-flush sequence. **Suggested revision:** State explicitly whether `[PLANNED]` rename and `design-log-publish` apply after clarify-driven p