ses (11)`. No duplicate harness names across `test-harnesses-*:` lines (checked).\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-security-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the branch diff and commit history for a read-only security-focused review. We won't write the TSV sidecar (read-only constraint); we'll include structured TSV rows in the response if needed.\n\nVerifying the CI workflow step label line number and whether `larch-logs` is typically ignored.\n\n\n- **Step review Step 3a tsv-fallback — collect-findings.sh inline-TSV recovery cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt warning (exit 0)**:\n  ```\nGathering the pre-computed diff and commit history for a read-only plan-fidelity review. `git log` and `git merge-base` are read-only.\n\nFetching exact line numbers for the CI step name and checking whether `docs/linting.md` still mentions `-j10`.\n\n## Plan fidelity review (branch vs `main`)\n\n**Commits** (`git merge-base HEAD main`..HEAD):\n\n- `8b2b3ca` Rebalance CI test-harness shards from 10 to 11 (closes #2252)\n- `7d3172e` chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41\n\n**Plan traceability (Makefile / CI / docs):** The rebalance commit matches the stated plan: `test-harnesses-11` on `.PHONY` and the umbrella; comment block references `#2252` and LPT; shards 1–11 match the planned prerequisite lists (including `test-harness-shards-coverage` first on shard 11); [`.github/workflows/ci.yaml`](.github/workflows/ci.yaml) matrix includes shard `11`; [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md) updates “ten”→“eleven”, branch-protection bullet for `test-harnesses (11)`, and the “Changing the shard count” section to `11`.\n\n**Read-only constraint:** Per your instruction, no files were written (including the `.tsv` sidecar). The TSV block below is inline for copy/paste if you still want a sidecar file locally.\n\n---\n\n"}
<TMPDIR>/codex-primary-plan-requirements-output.txt.sidecar:3070:./larch-logs/implement/086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41/execution-issues.ndjson:9:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"In-Scope Findings","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"1dd854b6f4d4bd2291a55da555b453fa025b7a8c83d16bdce07f00dd19919d38","body":"\n1. **`risk-integration` — Important** — [`.github/workflows/ci.yaml`](.github/workflows/ci.yaml):186 — The step name is still `Run test harnesses (shard ${{ matrix.shard }} of 10)` while the matrix now includes shard `11`. In the Actions UI and logs, shard 11 jobs are labeled “of 10,” which is wrong and can confuse triage when comparing matrix cells to docs. **Suggested fix:** Change the suffix to `of 11` (or remove the hard-coded total if you prefer a neutral label).\n\n2. **`code-quality` — Important** (plan / requirements) — [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md):22 — The **Usage → CI** bullet still says the matrix runs `make test-harnesses-1` through `make test-harnesses-10`, but the branch updates other prose to eleven shards and [`ci.yaml`](.github/workflows/ci.yaml) runs eleven cells. **Concrete scenario:** Someone reads only the top of `linting.md` and believes CI still stops at shard 10. **Suggested fix:** Update that phrase to `test-harnesses-11`.\n\n3. **`code-quality` — Important** — [`scripts/test-harness-shards-coverage.md`](scripts/test-harness-shards-coverage.md):26-27 — The script’s sibling contract still says the last partition-guard shard is `test-harnesses-10:` and that the umbrella spans `test-harnesses-1` through `test-harnesses-10`. After this change, the Makefile’s last shard is `test-harnesses-11`. **Scenario:** Contributors following the script’s `.md` neighbor doc get the wrong mental model for “last shard” and umbrella span. **Suggested fix:** Point at `test-harnesses-11` or describe “highest `N` discovered from the Makefile” without a stale literal.\n\n4. **`code-quality` — Nit** — [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md):42 — Parallel-local guidance still says `make -j10 test-harnesses` even though eleven shard targets exist. **Suggested fix:** Use `-j11` or wording like “up to the shard count.”\n\n5. **`code-quality` — Nit** — [`larch-logs/implement/086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41/manifest.json`](larch-logs/implement/086677CB-5DA8-4D45-9343-0C3506B2CE41/manifest.json):10 — The committed manifest has `\"status\": \"in-progress\"` and `\"pr_number\": null`, unlike the “committed alongside the PR” completed-run shape described in [`docs/run-logs.md`](docs/run-logs.md). **Scenario:** Anyone treating `larch-logs/` as a finished-run archive gets a mid-flight snapshot. **Suggested fix:** Either complete the run and flush a terminal manifest or omit this directory from the change set if it was accidental.\n\n**Plan verification (structure):** [`Makefile`](Makefile) adds `test-harnesses-11`, extends the umbrella and `.PHONY`, moves `test-harness-shards-coverage` to the first prerequisite of the new last shard, and rebalance comments reference #2252 as planned. [`docs/linting.md`](docs/linting.md) branch-protection and “Changing the shard count” sections were updated per plan, but the early **Usage** paragraph was not (finding 2). A duplicate-harness scan across all `test-harnesses-*:` prerequisite tokens returned no duplicates (read-only `awk` + `sort | uniq -d`).\n\n---\n\n"}
