<TMPDIR>/codex-primary-plan-requirements-output.txt.sidecar:3086:./larch-logs/implement/9C7CDB30-2B1E-45E4-B7EB-77EDC4557CB3/session-transcript.jsonl:102:{"turn":101,"role":"user","blocks":[{"type":"text","value":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked `/larch:fix-issue 2523` to fix GitHub issue #2523 in the `character-ai/larch` repository. Issue #2523 titled \"audit-runs skill: filter findings against in-flight/closed-with-version-window issues + narrow oos-category-mangle scan\" describes four related bugs in the `/audit-runs` skill (`.claude/skills/audit-runs/`). The user subsequently confirmed deletion of stray untracked files (`=` and `round`) to clean the working tree, enabling the fix to proceed. The fix-issue run delegated to `/implement --merge` and is now mid-execution, having created a feature branch and begun the inline design plan.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **larch `/fix-issue` skill**: orchestrates locking a GitHub issue, triaging it, classifying intent/complexity, and delegating to `/implement`\n   - **larch `/implement` skill**: full end-to-end pipeline: branch creation → inline plan → implementation → checks → commit → code review → version bump → PR → CI → merge\n   - **Dirty-tree pre-lock check**: `find-lock-issue.sh` runs `check-clean-tree.sh --fail-closed` before acquiring the GitHub comment lock; fails closed on dirty tree (exit 2) without touching GitHub state\n   - **Tracking issue adoption (Branch 2)**: `/implement --issue 2523` causes Step 0.5 to adopt the already-locked issue rather than creating a new tracking issue\n   - **SIMPLE workflow path**: task classified SIMPLE (approach is explicit in issue with code snippets) → skips `/design`, produces inline plan, proceeds directly to Step 2 implementation\n   - **Session tmpdirs**: `FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR` and `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR` are separate session directories for fix-issue and implement respectively\n   - **Round-trip detection**: `round-trip-detect.sh` checks if the issue title/body is an LLM-generated round-trip before renaming\n   - **`audit-scan-run.sh`**: shell script that runs all scans against one run-log directory, emits NDJSON output\n   - **`review-findings-full.jsonl`**: NDJSON file with per-finding payloads; fields include `phase`, `outcome`, `category`\n   - **`proposed_new_issues`** vs **`proposed_augmentations`**: classification of audit findings against open GitHub issues\n   - **version_window_checks**: planned new YAML frontmatter block to record decisions about closed-issue version filtering (C.2)\n   - **larch-log system**: `larch-log.sh` manages committed run logs under `larch-logs/implement/<RUN_ID>/`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`.claude/skills/audit-runs/SKILL.md`** (read fully)\n     - Contains the orchestration logic, scan descriptions, proposed_new_issues rules, and post-report user prompt\n     - **C.1 bug (line 105)**: `proposed_new_issues` currently excludes `^\\[IN PROGRESS\\]` titles from search, generating false-positive proposals for in-progress fixes\n     - **C.2**: No version-window filter for closed issues; only open issues searched\n     - **C.4**: No post-report session summary step exists\n     - Current buggy rule: `findings with no matching open issue (excluding titles matching ^\\[Run Logs Audit Report or ^\\[IN PROGRESS\\] when searching)`\n     - **C.1 fix**: Change so matching open issues (including [IN PROGRESS]) → snapshot with \"recurred this batch — pre-fix\" note, not proposed_new_issues; only `[Run Logs Audit Report ...]` excluded\n     - **C.4 fix**: Add step after per-finding walkthrough to post session summary comment to audit-report issue using `gh issue comment <N> --repo \"<repo>\" --body-file \"$TMPDIR/session-summary.md\"`\n   \n   - **`.claude/skills/audit-runs/scripts/audit-scan-run.sh`** (partially read — lines 185-210 confirmed)\n     - Contains `scan_oos_category_mangle()` function\n     - **C.3 bug**: Current implementation uses `select(.category != null)` which counts ALL phases including code-review accepted (by-design) and OOS blank rows\n     - Current buggy jq filter:\n       ```bash\n       count=$(jq -r 'select(.category != null) | .category' \"$jsonl\" 2>/dev/null \\\n           | grep -cvE '^(code-quality|risk-integration|correctness|architecture|security) || true)\n       ```\n     - Detail label says \"plan-review-phase rows with prose category\" but actually counts code-review too\n     - **C.3 fix** (from issue): \n       ```bash\n       count=$(jq -r 'select(\n           .phase == \"plan-review\" and\n           .outcome == \"accepted\" and\n           (.category // \"\") != \"\" and\n           ((.category // \"\") | test(\"^(code-quality|risk-integration|correctness|architecture|security)$\") | not)\n       ) | .id' \"$jsonl\" 2>/dev/null | wc -l | tr -d '[:space:]')\n       ```\n\n   - **`.claude/skills/audit-runs/scans.tsv`** (read fully)\n     - TSV with columns: name, type, pattern, expected_outcome, severity\n     - `oos-category-mangle` row currently: `jsonl-field | .category not in [\"code-quality\",\"risk-integration\",\"correctness\",\"architecture\",\"security\"] | all OOS category fields use canonical values | high`\n     - Needs update to reflect narrowed scope (plan-review accepted only)\n\n   - **`.claude/skills/audit-runs/scripts/test-audit-runs.sh`** (not yet read)\n     - Needs test fixtures and assertions for C.1, C.3, C.4\n     - C.1 test: code-review-accepted prose category → oos-category-mangle: pass\n     - C.3 test: plan-review-accepted prose category → oos-category-mangle: fail\n     - C.4 test: session summary posted after walkthrough\n\n   - **Session files**:\n     - `FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR=<TMPDIR>`\n     - `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR=<TMPDIR>`\n     - `$FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR/session-env.sh` — session env for fix-issue\n     - `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/session-env.sh` — session env for implement\n     - `$FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR/issue-details.txt` — full issue #2523 content\n     - `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/larch-logs/implement/9C7CDB30-2B1E-45E4-B7EB-77EDC4557CB3/manifest.json` — larch-log manifest\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Dirty working tree (first /fix-issue attempt)**: `find-lock-issue.sh` exited code 2 with \"Working tree is not clean. Commit or stash changes, then re-run /fix-issue.\" Two zero-byte untracked files `=` and `round` (accidental artifacts of a mistyped command, created 2026-05-21 11:44) caused this. Fixed by deleting them: `rm = round`. No GitHub state was touched.\n   - **Issue rename RENAMED=false at Step 0.5 of /implement**: Tracking issue title rename returned `RENAMED=false` — this is NOT an error. It's the idempotent case: `/fix-issue`'s `find-lock-issue.sh` already renamed the title to `[IN PROGRESS]` in Step 0, so `/implement`'s Branch 2 rename is a no-op.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Successfully cleaned working tree by removing stray files\n   - Successfully locked issue #2523 and set up both fix-issue and implement sessions\n   - Issue triaged as MATERIAL (all four bugs confirmed present in codebase)\n   - Classified as INTENT=PR, COMPLEXITY=SIMPLE\n   - Feature branch `sergey-zhupanov/fix-2523-audit-runs-filters` created from main\n   - Tracking issue adopted (Branch 2) with metadata comment posted\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/larch:fix-issue 2523` — initial invocation to fix issue #2523\n   - `clear git status` — user asked to see git status (interpreted as checking what was dirty)\n   - `yes` — confirmed deletion of the two stray empty files (`=` and `round`)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Complete `/implement` execution** for issue #2523 with all four sub-fixes:\n     - **C.1**: Update `proposed_new_issues` rule in `.claude/skills/audit-runs/SKILL.md` so open issues (including [IN PROGRESS]) → snapshot not propose; update LLM classify step in Orchestrator Flow\n     - **C.2**: Extend LLM classification step in SKILL.md to search open+closed issues with version-window logic and `version_window_checks` YAML frontmatter\n     - **C.3**: Fix `scan_oos_category_mangle()` in `audit-scan-run.sh` to use narrowed jq filter (plan-review + accepted + non-empty category + non-canonical); update `scans.tsv` row; fix detail label\n     - **C.4**: Add post-report session summary step to SKILL.md (compose markdown comment, post with `gh issue comment`)\n     - Update `test-audit-runs.sh` with tests for C.1, C.3, C.4\n   - **Continue /implement Steps 1 through 18**: inline plan → implementation → checks → commit → code review → version bump → PR → CI → merge\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The `/implement` orchestrator is currently at **Step 1 (design plan)**, specifically at the inline plan stage. The simplicity classification was completed (ROUTER_CLASSIFICATION=SIMPLE), the feature branch `sergey-zhupanov/fix-2523-audit-runs-filters` was created, and the relevant files (`SKILL.md` and `scans.tsv`) were read to inform the inline plan. The plan has not yet been written to disk (`$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/design-export/plan.txt`), and Step 2 (implementation) has not yet begun.\n\n   Key state:\n   - `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR=<TMPDIR>`\n   - `FIX_ISSUE_TMPDIR=<TMPDIR>`\n   - `RUN_ID=9C7CDB30-2B1E-45E4-B7EB-77EDC4557CB3`\n   - `ISSUE_NUMBER=2523`\n   - `BRANCH_NAME=sergey-zhupanov/fix-2523-audit-runs-filters`\n   - `REPO=character-ai/larch`\n   - `merge=true`, `hard_mode=false`, `auto_mode=false`, `ROUTER_CLASSIFICATION=SIMPLE`\n   - Codex and Cursor both available; implementer waterfall will select `coder=cursor`\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the `/implement` Step 1 inline plan: write the implementation plan to `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/design-export/plan.txt`, write the voting tally placeholder to `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/design-export/voting-tally.md`, then proceed through the Step 1 tail (larch-log batches, implementer waterfall selecting cursor, Step 1.r rebase checkpoint) and into Step 2 implementation.\n\n   From the most recent work: the orchestrator was at \"Now let me read the target files to produce the inline plan\" and had just finished reading both `SKILL.md` and `scans.tsv`. The next concrete action is to produce the plan content and write it to disk, then invoke the implementer (cursor) to make the four code changes (C.1–C.4) across the audit-runs skill files.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: <OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>/projects/-Users-zhupanov-larch6/ac150bee-acf1-4e73-992f-747faaa51e45.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]}
