<TMPDIR>/codex-primary-plan-requirements-output.txt.sidecar:3116:./larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/code-review-tally.json:1:{"schema_version":1,"phase":"code-review","batch":"code-review-tally","mode":"simple","rounds":1,"accepted_count":68,"rejected_count":0,"body":"# Review Round 1\n\n- Mode: `diff`\n- Accepted findings: 68\n- Rejected findings: 0\n\n## Accepted Findings\n\n### FINDING_1: **BLOCKING**, `risk-integration`, `larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json:1-20` plus sibling `plan-goals-test.md` and `plan-review-tally.json` (commit `c4a3b5d7`): The branch adds a committed implement run directory (manifest with `operator_cwd` / `operator_repo_root`, `status: in-progress`, issue `2187`, and plan artifacts). That is unrelated product noise for the sanitizer change, bloats the plugin repo, and ships another machine’s paths into every consumer checkout. **Concrete scenario:** Anyone cloning the repo gets this run snapshot in `larch-logs/` and the PR diff is dominated by operational data instead of the NDJSON guard. **Suggested fix:** Remove that directory from the branch (drop or rewrite the `chore(larch-logs): flush implement run …` commit) so only the intentional script/doc/test changes remain.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-edge-cases-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **BLOCKING**, `risk-integration`, `larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json:1-20` plus sibling `plan-goals-test.md` and `plan-review-tally.json` (commit `c4a3b5d7`): The branch adds a committed implement run directory (manifest with `operator_cwd` / `operator_repo_root`, `status: in-progress`, issue `2187`, and plan artifacts). That is unrelated product noise for the sanitizer change, bloats the plugin repo, and ships another machine’s paths into every consumer checkout. **Concrete scenario:** Anyone cloning the repo gets this run snapshot in `larch-logs/` and the PR diff is dominated by operational data instead of the NDJSON guard. **Suggested fix:** Remove that directory from the branch (drop or rewrite the `chore(larch-logs): flush implement run …` commit) so only the intentional script/doc/test changes remain.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_2: **Commits reviewed** (`git merge-base HEAD main..HEAD`): `9e392b54 Harden NDJSON batch sanitizers`, `c4a3b5d7 chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4`.\n- **Reviewer**: \n- **Concern**: \n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_3: **Important** (`risk-integration`) [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json):1-20, [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md):1-37, [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json):1 (commit `c4a3b5d7 chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 018DCD66-...`): The branch diff includes committed `/implement` run artifacts under `larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-...`, which are **not** listed in the implementation plan’s “Files to modify” or in the feature description’s deliverables (those only name `scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`, `scripts/larch-log-batches.md`, `scripts/test-larch-log.sh`, `scripts/test-larch-log.md`, plus call-site audit). A reviewer bisecting `main..HEAD` therefore sees an unrelated second commit and extra tree churn beside the sanitizer/doc/test work, which obscures the intended functional change set and can create needless merge/rebase conflicts. **Suggested fix:** Remove that commit (or otherwise exclude these paths from the PR) so the branch contains only the planned `scripts/*` edits.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-plan-fidelity-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **Important** (`risk-integration`) [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json):1-20, [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md):1-37, [larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json):1 (commit `c4a3b5d7 chore(larch-logs): flush implement run 018DCD66-...`): The branch diff includes committed `/implement` run artifacts under `larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-...`, which are **not** listed in the implementation plan’s “Files to modify” or in the feature description’s deliverables (those only name `scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`, `scripts/larch-log-batches.md`, `scripts/test-larch-log.sh`, `scripts/test-larch-log.md`, plus call-site audit). A reviewer bisecting `main..HEAD` therefore sees an unrelated second commit and extra tree churn beside the sanitizer/doc/test work, which obscures the intended functional change set and can create needless merge/rebase conflicts. **Suggested fix:** Remove that commit (or otherwise exclude these paths from the PR) so the branch contains only the planned `scripts/*` edits.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_4: **Important** `code-quality` (requirements: scope) — [`larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json:1-20`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json), [`plan-goals-test.md:1-37`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md), [`plan-review-tally.json:1`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json): The branch bundles a second commit that adds a fresh implement run snapshot (manifest still `in-progress`, local `operator_*` paths, and plan/tally copies) together with the sanitizer and test changes. That is unrelated surface area for a “harden NDJSON sanitizers” change, forces reviewers to treat run-log policy and PII-ish paths as part of the same merge, and is not called for in the feature description. **Suggested fix:** Drop these paths from the feature PR (or split a dedicated “flush run log” PR) so the merge stays limited to [`scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`](scripts/larch-log-batches.sh), [`scripts/larch-log-batches.md`](scripts/larch-log-batches.md), [`scripts/test-larch-log.sh`](scripts/test-larch-log.sh), and [`scripts/test-larch-log.md`](scripts/test-larch-log.md).\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-structure-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 1. **Important** `code-quality` (requirements: scope) — [`larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json:1-20`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/manifest.json), [`plan-goals-test.md:1-37`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-goals-test.md), [`plan-review-tally.json:1`](larch-logs/implement/018DCD66-69F0-450C-B351-D3A2F817B0D4/plan-review-tally.json): The branch bundles a second commit that adds a fresh implement run snapshot (manifest still `in-progress`, local `operator_*` paths, and plan/tally copies) together with the sanitizer and test changes. That is unrelated surface area for a “harden NDJSON sanitizers” change, forces reviewers to treat run-log policy and PII-ish paths as part of the same merge, and is not called for in the feature description. **Suggested fix:** Drop these paths from the feature PR (or split a dedicated “flush run log” PR) so the merge stays limited to [`scripts/larch-log-batches.sh`](scripts/larch-log-batches.sh), [`scripts/larch-log-batches.md`](scripts/larch-log-batches.md), [`scripts/test-larch-log.sh`](scripts/test-larch-log.sh), and [`scripts/test-larch-log.md`](scripts/test-larch-log.md).\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_5: