e asked to commit new `larch-logs/...` artifacts. **Concrete scenario**: Merging ships unrelated churn; `manifest.json` records `operator_cwd` / `operator_repo_root` as absolute paths and `status: \"in-progress\"`, which is noise for consumers and slightly widens accidental disclosure of machine layout. **Suggested fix**: Remove these paths from the PR (or split into a separate, explicitly justified run-log commit per repo policy); keep the functional diff limited to `scripts/` as scoped.\n- **Suggested revision**: Address the concern above.\n\n### FINDING_7: **Latent** `risk-integration` — Feature text asks to audit [`scripts/append-execution-issue.sh`](scripts/append-execution-issue.sh) and [`scripts/append-tool-failure.sh`](scripts/append-tool-failure.sh) for “valid JSON”; the diff does not add comments or tests tying them to NDJSON. **Plan-correctness / requirements**: Those scripts append **markdown** into a caller-chosen `LOG_FILE` via awk ([`append-execution-issue.sh`](scripts/append-execution-issue.sh):118-156); [`append-tool-failure.sh`](scripts/append-tool-failure.sh):131-148 builds markdown and calls `append-execution-issue.sh`. They do **not** call `larch-log.sh append` on `execution-issues.ndjson`. **Concrete scenario**: A follow-up “fix” mistakenly rewrites them to emit raw NDJSON into the markdown log. **Suggested fix**: In the PR description, one line stating NDJSON append is only via `larch-log.sh` / orchestrator / [`scripts/implement-finalize.sh`](scripts/implement-finalize.sh) (jq/python path ~256-357) so the audit is closed without code churn.\n- **Reviewer**: cursor-specialist-correctness-output.txt\n- **Concern**: 2. **Latent** `risk-integration` — Feature text asks to audit [`scripts/append-execution-issue.sh`](scripts/append-execution-issue.sh) and [`scripts/append-tool-failure.sh`](scripts/append-tool-failure.sh) for “valid JSON”; the diff does not add comments or tests tying them to NDJSON. **Plan-correctness / requirements**: Those scripts