<TMPDIR>/codex-primary-plan-requirements-output.txt.sidecar:3199:./larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/execution-issues.ndjson:2:{"phase":"implement","step":"7a","category":"In-Scope Findings","source":"execution-issues.md pre-bump","source_sha256":"911e07a7f90cf3a0d8dc9dbc2a65cf927bcdb8ce4795edcb44f959d34cfcbaf4","body":"\n1. **Important** `correctness` [Implementation plan §“Edge Cases” / `prefix_records` behavior] — The plan states the `user:attachment` branch must **not** set `included_initial` so a plain-text initial user (when it appears **before** attachment in the parent chain) can still be captured as `user:initial`. The implementation sets `included_initial = True` inside the `user:attachment` branch at [scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:332-335](scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py). Concrete impact: any later plain `user` bubble in the same prefix walk no longer qualifies for `user:initial` once an attachment user has been seen, which diverges from the plan’s explicit `included_initial` story (even though it matches [scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh:135-146](scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh) `write_attachment_then_text_fixture`). Suggested fix: either remove the `included_initial` assignment from the attachment branch and adjust tests/docs, or revise the plan/contract bullet so it matches the shipped semantics.\n\n2. **Important** `risk-integration` [Implementation plan §“Files to Modify”] — The plan lists only four paths (`scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py`, `scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh`, `scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.md`, `scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.md`). The branch also adds committed implement run artifacts under [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/) (e.g. [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/manifest.json](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/manifest.json), [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/code-review-tally.json](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/code-review-tally.json), [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/review-findings-full.md](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/review-findings-full.md), [larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/plan-goals-test.md](larch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/plan-goals-test.md)). That is out-of-band versus the stated file list and couples the feature to a specific run id. Suggested fix: drop these from the feature branch unless a documented run-log policy explicitly requires them, or extend the plan/PR scope to justify them.\n\n3. **Nit** `correctness` [Implementation plan §1 `content_to_text()`] — The plan prescribes `json.dumps(item, …)` for `tool_result` / `tool_use` blocks to preserve all fields. The implementation instead routes non-`text` dict/list blocks through `summarize_attachment_block()` ([scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:334-367](scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py)), emitting `type` plus `payload_sha256` only in rendered/digested prefix material. This is consistent with the updated contract in [scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.md](scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.md) and [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md), but it is a literal deviation from the pasted implementation plan text and from the plan’s stated side effect about `\"tool_use_id\"` appearing in flattened `entry_content`. Suggested fix: amend the authoritative plan/spec to describe redacted summaries (or revert to full JSON if that remains the source of truth).\n\n**Plan completeness (positive, no severity):** `_is_attachment_bearing` dict-shaped `message.content` handling ([scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:304-305](scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py)), extra harness scenarios (`write_attachment_dict_fixture`, `write_tool_use_mutation_fixture`, `write_attachment_then_text_fixture`), and branched `parentUuid: sys1` mutation shapes ([scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh:75-132](scripts/test-cache-key-runtime-audit.sh)) satisfy or exceed the plan’s functional intent (attachment-bearing users in the stable prefix, `CACHE-INVALIDATING` on same-slot drift, redacted reports).\n\n**Commits on branch since merge-base with `main`:** `3e57ba64` Fix stable-prefix audit…; `d525a4bc` / `f02d77e1` chore(larch-logs)…; `57e52ef5` / `d6546c31` Address code review feedback.\n\n---\n\nRead-only mode: TSV sidecar file was not written. Records below use tabs; replace literal newlines in fields with space if you ingest them.\n\n```tsv\nschema_version\tscope\tseverity\tfocus_area\tlocation\twhat\tscenario_or_breakage\tsuggested_fix\n1\tin_scope\timportant\tcorrectness\tscripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:332-335\tuser:attachment sets included_initial=True, contradicting plan Edge Cases bullet\tPlan promised attachment path does not flip included_initial so earlier/later plain user:initial eligibility matches that story; shipped code suppresses later plain user:initial after an attachment user in the same chain walk\tRemove included_initial mutation from attachment branch and retest, or update plan/contract to the new semantics\n1\tin_scope\timportant\trisk-integration\tlarch-logs/implement/C5B28F06-C105-4ECC-B99A-59C3023BFB0E/ (manifest.json, code-review-tally.json, review-findings-full.md, plan-goals-test.md, plan-review-tally.json)\tCommitted implement run artifacts not listed under plan Files to Modify\tFeature PR scope exceeds the four planned paths and pins private review metadata into version control\tRemove larch-logs changes from the feature branch or expand the plan/PR scope with an explicit run-log justification\n1\tin_scope\tnit\tcorrectness\tscripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.py:281-367\tcontent_to_text uses summarized attachment blocks, not full JSON.dumps for tool_result/tool_use per plan §1\tLiteral plan-to-code mismatch on serialization shape; docs/SECURITY describe redaction instead\tReconcile the written implementation plan with scripts/cache-key-runtime-audit.md or restore full JSON if that remains authoritative\n```\n  ```\n"}
